# Overview & Installation

## Overview

GMWidgets is a SuperCollider (SC) API which provides a Graphical User Interface (GUI) to the GMDefs API.

Its purpose is to allow you to build your own musical software with ease, letting you decide how it should look like, what kind of controls you'd rather use, and your favorite colors.

## Dependencies & technical purpose

GMWidgets relies on the Graphical Module quark, that provides new widgets to SC. You can install it by evaluating `Quarks.install("GraphicalModule");`. Keep it up-to-date!

GMWidgets doesn't make much sense without GMDefs. As an example, GMDefs allows you to get a synth using `var mySynth = ~gmDefs.getSynth("PresetName")`. You can then control this synth using the commands GMDefs provides. But if you'd rather have a GUI to control the synth, GMWidgets is here to make your life easier (depending on the level of customisation you need).

`var mySynthView = ~gmWidgets.getSynthView(mySynth)` will give you a ready-to-use GUI to make that oscillator go wild! This is also true for the other GMDefs objects (like the Player).

If you're still insatisfied with the result, you can make your own synth view using the built-in widgets (buttons, slider, ...).

## Using GMWidgets

Download the latest version using git, and create a symlink to the directory within your project.

At runtime, simply execute `gmWidgets.scd`. This will push the extension into a global variable, `~gmWidgets`, which gives you access to its functionalities.

Here's a template that will load both GMDefs and GMWidgets :

```
var folder = thisProcess.nowExecutingPath.dirname;

var loadDependencies;
loadDependencies = {
	if(File.exists(folder ++ "/GMDefs/")) {
		this.executeFile(
			folder ++
			"/GMDefs/gmDefs.scd"
		);
	} {
		"GMDefs directory not found".warn;
	};
	if(File.exists(folder ++ "/GMWidgets/")) {
		this.executeFile(
			folder ++
			"/GMWidgets/gmWidgets.scd"
		);
	} {
		"GMWidgets directory not found".warn;
	};
};

loadDependencies.value;

```

