# Core concepts

## Signals

### Using signals

GMWidgets uses a signal system to provide as much flexibility as possible :

```
(
var selector = ~gmWidgets.getSelector;
selector.states(["A", "B", "C"]);
selector.state(0);
selector.connectSignal(
	\_stateChanged, { |state|
		state.postln;
	}
);
selector.doFront;
)
```

Here, we're instantiating a selector, which, when pressed, emits a `\_stateChanged` signal, passing its new state as argument.

With the `connectSignal` method, we define what action should take place when the signal is emitted : the chosen `Function` will be called, with the argument(s), every time the selector emits the chosen signal.

See the views individual documentation for a list of their individual built-in signals.

It is possible to connect any number of Function to the signal :

```
(
var states = ["A", "B", "C"];
var selector = ~gmWidgets.getSelector;
selector.states(states);
selector.state(0);
selector.connectSignal(
	\_stateChanged, { |state|
		state.postln;
	}
);
selector.connectSignal(
	\_stateChanged, { |state|
		states[state].postln;
	}
);
selector.doFront;
)
```

When not needed anymore, the Function should be disconnected from the signal. This necessitates storing the Function inside a Variable (which is a good practice anyway) :

```
(
var states = ["A", "B", "C"];

var selector = ~gmWidgets.getSelector;

var postNewState = { |state|
	states[state].postln;
};

selector.states(states);
selector.state(0);

selector.connectSignal(
	\_stateChanged,
	postNewState
);

selector.disconnectSignal(
	\_stateChanged,
	postNewState
);

selector.doFront;
)
```

You can also disconnect all Functions from a signal at once, or completely disconnect every signals :

```
selector.clearSignal(\_stateChanged);
selector.clearAllSignals;
```

### Creating your own signals

Now if you're willing to code your own interface, you can simply copy-paste the signal code block to your prototype, declare the signal dictionary in the `init` method, then use `self.emitSignal(\mySignal, arg);` to do whatever you'd like :

```
init: { |self|
	self[\signals] = ();
	[...]
},

[...]

doSomething: { |self|
	self.emitSignal(\mySignal, arg);
},

[...]

//---------//
// SIGNALS //
emitSignal: { |self, symbol, args = nil|
	if(self[\signals].includesKey(symbol)) {
		if(args.isNil) {
			self[\signals][symbol].value;
		} {
			self[\signals][symbol].value(args);
		};
	};
},

connectSignal: { |self, symbol, function|
	if(self[\signals][symbol].isNil) {
		self[\signals][symbol] = FunctionList();
	};
	self[\signals][symbol].addFunc(function);
	self
},

disconnectSignal: { |self, symbol, function|
	if(self[\signals].includesKey(symbol)) {
		self[\signals][symbol].removeFunc(function);
	};
},

clearSignal: { |self, symbol|
	self[\signals].removeAt(symbol);
},

clearAllSignals: { |self|
	self[\signals].clear;
	self[\signals] = ();
},
```

