# Prototypes documentation

## Global methods and variables

Some variables and methods are used by the vast majority of the prototypes. Please note that methods are not inherited, they're declared within the file itself to retain complete modularity.

To access a variable, use the `prototype[\variable]` syntax. To call a method, use the `prototype.method(arg)` syntax.

You should be familiar with those variables and methods to use any part of GMWidgets.

### Signals

See the Signals documentation above.

- `[\signals]` an IdentityDictionary

- `emitSignal(Symbol signal, args arguments)`

- `connectSignal(Symbol signal, Function func)`

- `disconnectSignal(Symbol signal, Function func)`

- `clearSignal(Symbol signal)`

- `clearAllSignals`

### View

- `[\view]` The prototype itself is not the view. For example, if you need to insert the view inside a layout, do it like so : `HLayout().add(prototype[\view]);`.

- `setStyles(GMStyle style, GMStyle textStyle, GMStyle widgetStyle)`

Behaves differently depending on the view.

### Misc

- `init`

Creates, intializes and returns the prototype.

- `doFront`

Creates a new window embedding the view. Hitting CmdPeriod will remove the prototype (and thus the window). This is a debugging tool, create your own window when designing your project.

- `doRemove`

Deletes the prototype and its children. It will be garbage collected. Don't forget to call it for every prototype you created when your process ends!

