## Widgets

Widgets are GUI base building blocks, such as buttons, sliders, etc. They're basically an enhancement of the Grapical Module widgets : they implement the signal system, some window compostion functionalities, and specific methods that are relevant to the widget type.

---
### Switch

A multi-state button that increments its state on each press (and resets back to the beginning at the end). See Graphical Module : GMSwitchButton.

#### Methods

- `~gmWidgets.getSwitch;`

- `state(Integer index)`

- `states(Array states)` ```["A", "B", "C"]```

or (svg is optionnal) :

```
[
	(
		string: "A",
		color: Color.rand,
		fontColor: Color.black,
		svg: "path/to/a/file.svg"
	),
	(
		string: "B",
		color: Color.rand,
		fontColor: Color.black,
		svg: "path/to/a/file.svg"
	),
]
```

#### Signals

- `\_stateChanged { Integer newState }`

#### Template

```
var switchStates, switch, switchAction;

switchStates = ["A", "B", "C"];
switchAction = { |state|
	state.postln;
};
switch = ~gmWidgets.getSwitch
.states(switchStates)
.connectSignal(
	\_stateChanged,
	switchAction
);
```


