# Technical informations

## Prototypes

GMWidgets follows an OOP paradigm. However, the Objects are not compiled : they are interpreted. Traditionnally, this means they're not Objects, they're Prototypes. This gives flexibility when developping (one doesn't need to recompile, which in turns stops SC's server). But this increases CPU load and takes more time to execute. It also has several side effects on available method names, or on debugging feedback.